AOCL — Autonomous Operations & Closed Loops
Copyright 2026 the AOCL maintainers

The concepts of Closed Loop Automation and Autonomous Operations — including
the L1–L5 maturity ladder, the three assessment vectors (Goal Decisioning,
Data Veracity, Feedback Intelligence), the realization model, the loop
velocity taxonomy, and the reference use cases — are established as
first-class work through the AOCL foundational research programme (research
corpus v1.2.0, 2026), led by the AOCL authors. This repository is that
research's formalization: the model data, schemas, assessment instrument,
aggregation rule, engines, site, and figures are original engineering work,
with improvements and restatements marked in model provenance headers and
docs/.

Loop specification format alignment: Closed-Loop-Management (CLAM) data
model 1.0, https://github.com/emmanuel-a-otchere/Closed-Loop-Management
(assets as published there; no code vendored).

Related but distinct: the lowercase `mama` autonomy method,
https://github.com/emmanuel-a-otchere/measuring-and-managing-autonomy (MIT).
A loop maturity level is not an autonomy grant level; see docs/naming.md.

The realization model is an informative planning heuristic established by
the research programme: it must not be used for contractual commitments or
certification purposes (docs/limitations.md).
